From cbbd2f8b760ff2b6ec15ef381849f3d8c87398e1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: devbotbo <7118.eth@proton.me>
Date: Mon, 7 Sep 2026 20:24:14 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Add blind-relay session table, client JWK validation and
 address-bound nonce

A relay session is one whose direct_post.jwt response is encrypted to a
key the client generated, so the service can only store the JWE, never
open it. This adds the module that owns the session table, the P-256
public JWK validation (no d, on-curve point, ECDH-ES/enc only), the
nonce formula hex(sha256(address20 || challenge)) with pinned vectors,
and one-time pickup semantics. build_client_metadata is opened to the
crate so a relay request advertises the same client_metadata shape as
the default path with only the key swapped.
